From: LixNix <105106115+LixNix@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: flow_calibrator: resolve percentage line width per extruder

Orca states line widths as a percentage of the nozzle diameter. Resolve it
against the calibrated extruder's diameter instead of failing the range
check and falling back to the built-in flow parameters.

Original work by @LixNix (patch 03 of the U1 2.0.0.205
nozzle-map fix), rebased onto firmware-extended without changes.

--- a/klippy/extras/flow_calibrator.py
+++ b/klippy/extras/flow_calibrator.py
@@ -768,7 +768,16 @@
                         nozzle_volume_type == 'high_flow':
                     gcode_print_accel = gcode_parameters['outer_wall_accel_hf']
 
-                if gcode_parameters['line_width'] < 0.00001 or gcode_parameters['line_width'] > nozzle_diameter * 2 or \
+                # Orca states line widths as a percentage of the nozzle diameter. Resolve it here,
+                # where the diameter of the extruder being calibrated is known; without this the
+                # value never passes the range check below and every job silently falls back to the
+                # built-in flow parameters.
+                gcode_line_width = gcode_parameters['line_width']
+                gcode_line_width_percent = gcode_parameters.get('line_width_percent', 0)
+                if gcode_line_width < 0.00001 and gcode_line_width_percent > 0.00001:
+                    gcode_line_width = nozzle_diameter * gcode_line_width_percent / 100.0
+
+                if gcode_line_width < 0.00001 or gcode_line_width > nozzle_diameter * 2 or \
                         gcode_parameters['layer_height'] < 0.00001 or gcode_parameters['layer_height'] > nozzle_diameter * 1.1 or \
                         gcode_max_vol_speed < 0.00001 or gcode_max_vol_speed > 1000.0 or \
                         gcode_print_accel < 0.00001 or gcode_print_accel > 100000.0 or \
@@ -776,7 +785,7 @@
                         gcode_temp < extruder.heater.min_extrude_temp or gcode_temp > extruder.heater.max_temp:
                     raise
 
-                area_line = gcode_parameters['layer_height'] * (gcode_parameters['line_width'] - gcode_parameters['layer_height'] * ( \
+                area_line = gcode_parameters['layer_height'] * (gcode_line_width - gcode_parameters['layer_height'] * ( \
                                 1.0 - 3.1415926 / 4.0))
                 area_filament = 0.875 * 0.875 * 3.1415926
 
